1.File System Space Management
BEGIN
STEP 1: Set disk limit = 80%
STEP 2: Check current disk usage
STEP 3: IF disk usage > 80% THEN
STEP 4:     Find all log files
STEP 5:     Sort log files by size
STEP 6:     Select the largest log file
STEP 7:     Delete or compress the file
STEP 8:     Check disk usage again
STEP 9:     IF disk usage <= 80% THEN
STEP 10:        STOP
STEP 11:      ENDIF
STEP 12:    Repeat steps 6–10
STEP 13: ENDIF
STEP 14: END
2.Priority-Based CPU Scheduling
BEGIN
STEP 1. Input the list of processes
STEP 2. Sort processes by priority
STEP 3. Select the highest-priority process
STEP 4. Allocate CPU to the process
STEP 5. Execute the process
STEP 6. IF process is not completed THEN
STEP 7.     Reduce its priority
STEP 8.     Add it back to the process list
STEP 9. ENDIF
STEP 10. Repeat steps 3–9 until all processes are completed
STEP 11. END
3. RAM Allocation for Virtual Machines
BEGIN
STEP 1. Set total RAM = 16 GB
STEP 2. Reserve 4 GB for the host system
STEP 3. Calculate available RAM
STEP 4. Input number of VMs
STEP 5. Set minimum RAM = 2 GB
STEP 6. Select a VM
STEP 7. IF available RAM >= 2 GB THEN
STEP 8.     Allocate 2 GB to the VM
STEP 9.     Reduce available RAM by 2 GB
STEP 10. ELSE
STEP 11.     Display "Insufficient memory"
STEP 12. ENDIF
STEP 13. Repeat steps 6–12 for all VMs
STEP 14. END
4. Hypervisor Selection
BEGIN
STEP 1.Input performance requirement
STEP 2. Input budget
STEP 3. Input hardware access
STEP 4. IF performance is HIGH AND hardware access is TRUE THEN
STEP 5.     Select Type 1 Hypervisor
STEP 6. ELSE IF budget is LOW THEN
STEP 7.     Select Type 2 Hypervisor
STEP 8. ELSE
STEP 9.     Select Type 1 Hypervisor
STEP 10. ENDIF
STEP 11. Display selected hypervisor
STEP 12.END
5. CPU and Memory Resource Limiting
BEGIN
STEP 1. Input the list of applications
STEP 2. Select an application
STEP 3. Create a resource control group
STEP 4. Set CPU limit
STEP 5. Set memory limit
STEP 6. Assign the application to the group
STEP 7. Repeat steps 2–6 for all applications
STEP 8. END
